            <ArticleTitle>Role of cystoscopy and hydrodistention in the diagnosis of interstitial cystitis/bladder pain syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>624-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3978/j.issn.2223-4683.2015.09.04</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>There are controversies about whether cystoscopy with or without hydrodistention (HD) plays a role in the diagnosis and treatment of interstitial cystitis/bladder pain syndrome (IC/BPS). We reviewed the recommendations of various societies and associations of greater impact in this complex disease, analyzing the indications, technique, findings and complications of this procedure.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
